<title>LITHUANIA: LITHUANIA - AVERAGE YIELD DOWN ON 91-DAY T-BILLS.</title>
<headline>LITHUANIA - AVERAGE YIELD DOWN ON 91-DAY T-BILLS.</headline>
<dateline>VILNIUS 1997-08-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average yield at an auction</p>
<p>of 91-day Treasury bills fell on Monday and demand exceeded</p>
<p>supply, the central bank said.</p>
<p>All amounts are in millions of litas.</p>
<p> MATURITY   AV YIELD   LAST TIME   MIN/MAX   ISSUE  BID  SOLD</p>
<p> 91-day     7.32	 8.22	 7.10/7.47  30   82.726  30</p>
<p>The settlement date for today's auction is August 14 and the</p>
<p>bills mature on November 13.</p>
<p>The next T-bill auction will be held on August 19, when 30</p>
<p>million litas of 182-day paper will be offered.</p>
<p>-- Andrius Vilkancas, Vilnius newsroom +370 2 223 517</p>
</text>
